	<input type=checkbox name=ratio> also plot fragmentation function ratios (2/1, 3/1, 4/1)<br>

	<p>
	<input type=submit value="Make the Plot/Calculation ">
	<input type=reset value="Reset the Form">
	<p>
	</form>
<b>Remarks</b>
<ul>
<li> Mind that some species are not available for all sets!
<li> "Neutral cluster" means pi0+eta. The FF set chosen is that of pi0 (eta FF is given by the AESSS fit).
</ul>

	<b>References</b>
<ul>
<li>	AESSS, C. Aidala, F. Ellinghaus, R. Sassot, J. Seele, M. Stratmann, <a href="http://arXiv.org/abs/1009.6145">arXiv:1009.6145</a><br>

<li>	AKK05, S. Albino, B. A. Kniehl and G. Kramer,  Nucl. Phys. B725 (2005) 181 <a href="http://arXiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0502188">hep-ph/0502188</a>; Nucl. Phys. B734 (2006) 50 <a href="http://arXiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0510173">hep-ph/0510173</a><br>

<li>	AKK08, S. Albino, B. A. Kniehl and G. Kramer,  Nucl. Phys. B803 (2008) 42
	  <a href="http://arXiv.org/abs/0803.2768">0803.2768</a><br>

<li>	BFG, L. Bourhis, M. Fontannaz and J.-P. Guillet,  Eur. Phys. J. C2 (1998)
	  529 <a href="http://arXiv.org/abs/hep-ph/9704447">hep-ph/9704447</a><br>

<li>	BFGW, L. Bourhis, M. Fontannaz, J.-P. Guillet and M. Werlen,  Eur. Phys. J. C19
	  (2001) 89 <a href="http://arXiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0009101">
	  hep-ph/0009101</a><br>

<li>	BKK, J. Binnewies, B. A. Kniehl and G. Kramer,  Z. Phys. C65 (1995) 471
	  <a href="http://arXiv.org/abs/hep-ph/9407347">hep-ph/9407347</a><br>

<li>	DSS, D. de Florian, R. Sassot and M. Stratmann,  Phys. Rev. D75 (2007) 114010
	  <a href="http://arXiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0703242">hep-ph/0703242</a>; Phys. Rev. D76 (2007) 074033  <a href="http://arXiv.org/abs/0707.1506">0707.1506</a>;<br>

<li>	  DSV, D. de Florian, M. Stratmann and W. Vogelsang,  Phys. Rev. D57 (1998)
	  5811 <a href="http://arXiv.org/abs/hep-ph/9711387">
	  hep-ph/9711387</a><br>

<li>	HKNS, M. Hirai, S. Kumano, T. H. Nagai and K. Sudoh,  Phys. Rev. D75 (2007)
	  094009 <a href="http://arXiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0702250">hep-ph/0702250</a><br>

<li>	KKP, B. A. Kniehl, G. Kramer and B. P&ouml;tter,  Nucl. Phys. B582 (2000)
	  514 <a href="http://arXiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0010289">hep-ph/0010289</a><br>

<li>	KKKS08, T. Kneesch, B. A. Kniehl, G. Kramer, and I. Schienbein, Nucl. Phys. B799 (2008) 34 <a href="http://arXiv.org/abs/0712.0481">0712.0481</a><br>

<li>	S. Kretzer,  Phys. Rev. D62 (2000) 054001
	  <a href="http://arXiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0003177">hep-ph/0003177</a>
</ul>
